 "source_type": "instagram",
 "source_url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/De4aGojBRSc/",
 "title": "5 Editing Layers to Improve Reel Engagement",
 "topic": "content creation",
 "summary": "Kien Nguyen demonstrates how building up editing layers transforms static raw video into an engaging reel. Combining captions, camera zooms, graphics, and sound design holds viewer attention and increases retention.",
 "key_points": [
  "Raw Video: Plain talking-head video without visuals changing is easy for viewers to scroll past.",
  "Captions: Allow viewers to follow along with sound off and give their eyes something to track.",
  "Zooms: Small punch-ins/outs on key words keep the frame moving and prevent a static shot look.",
  "Graphics: Visualizing mentioned apps, numbers, or topics helps viewers process information faster.",
  "BGM & SFX: Background music sets the mood (keep volume low below voiceover) and sound effects emphasize visual cuts.",
  "Editing Priority: If short on time, prioritize captions and zooms first, adding graphics and sound design later."
 ],
 "content": "POST TEXT:\nWhat each layer is actually doing ↓\n\n1️⃣ Raw\nThis is just you talking. The idea can be great, but with nothing changing on screen it’s really easy to scroll past.\n\n2️⃣ Captions\nPlenty of people watch with the sound off. Captions let them follow along anyway, and give their eyes something to do while you talk.\n\n3️⃣ Zoom In & Out\nSmall punch ins on the words that matter keep the frame moving, so a talking head stops looking like one long static shot.\n\n4️⃣ Graphics\nIf you mention a number or an app, put it on screen. People get the point faster when they can see it.\n\n5️⃣ BGM & SFX\nA quiet music bed sets the mood, and a sound effect on each cut or reveal makes it hit. Keep the music low so it never fights your voice.\n\nEvery layer in this video uses the exact same take. The only thing that changes is the edit, and that’s what gets people to watch to the end and send it to someone.\n\nStart with captions and zooms, and add the rest when you have time.\n\n🔁 Share this with a creator who needs to hear this\n👣 Follow @kienobifilms for more practical editing tips\n\n#videoediting #reelstips #contentcreator\n\nTRANSCRIPT:\n\"Never post another reel without fixing this.\"\n\nTEXT ON SCREEN:\n- Raw vs Edited\n- Raw, Captions, Zoom In & Out, Graphics, BGM & SFX\n- Never post another reel without fixing this.",
